<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates dip across the board.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates dip across the board.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) edged lower across all maturities, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Banks adjusted their swap rates to take into account the strong inflows of dollars streaming into the country's stock market which has been posting record highs, traders said.</p>
<p>The dollars are to be changed to pesos which will add liquidity to the market, they said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.</p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>JAN 30 JAN 29</p>
<p>    1 W		9  3/4		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9  3/4		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		9  3/4		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 M		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9 13/16		 10</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  3/8		 10  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		31-Jan		  30-Jan</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
